# Overlapped Phase 2 Tiling Plan

## Goal

Overlap controller data movement with PE computation in phase 2.
Three activities can run concurrently because they touch different
SPM regions:

1. PE P2 compute on P2_BUF_X
2. Controller magic 15a reading P2_BUF_Y and loading FIN0_T
3. Controller magic 15b writing back FIN0_U to MM

## SPM Layout (per PE, 8192 words)

```
[0..1279]    P2 buf A  (P2_BASE)
[1280..2559] P2 buf B  (P2B_BASE)
[2560..4287] FIN0 tile X (FIN0_BASE)
[4288..6015] FIN0 tile Y (FIN0B_BASE)
[6016..8191] Q + GS sequences (interleaved, read-only)
```

## Current Non-Overlapped Flow

```
loop:
  magic 14 bufA    → load tiles from A queue into P2 bufA
  PE P2 bufA       → extend wavefront, produce fin0/fin1 diags
  magic 15 bufA    → writeback pushed/intv/fin1 to MM,
                     load fin0 data into FIN0 tile X
  PE FIN0 X        → hash check + char match
  magic 18 X       → writeback FIN0 results (A/B/HA) to MM
  [multipass loop if needed]

  magic 14 bufB    → load tiles
  PE P2 bufB       → extend
  magic 15 bufB    → writeback + load FIN0 tile X
  PE FIN0 X        → hash check
  magic 18 X       → writeback
  [multipass]

  magic 14 bufA    → load tiles
  if empty → exit
  jump loop
```

Key property: magic 15 runs AFTER PE P2 finishes on the SAME
buffer. magic 18 writes HA back to MM BEFORE the next magic 15
loads HA for the next diag. Everything is sequential.

## Overlapped Flow (from phase2TilingPrompt.txt)

Two P2 buffers (A, B) and two FIN0 tiles (X, Y). Each half
overlaps controller work with PE computation:

```
HALF_A:
  set_PC PE_P2 bufA           ← PE computes on bufA
  magic 15a: read bufB → X    ← reads PREVIOUS P2 results [OVERLAP]
  sync PE
  set_PC PE_FIN0 X            ← PE does hash check on X
  magic 14: load bufB         ← loads NEXT tiles [OVERLAP]
  magic 15b: writeback Y      ← writes PREVIOUS FIN0 results [OVERLAP]
  sync PE

HALF_B:
  set_PC PE_P2 bufB           ← PE computes on bufB
  magic 15a: read bufA → Y    ← reads PREVIOUS P2 results [OVERLAP]
  sync PE
  set_PC PE_FIN0 Y            ← PE does hash check on Y
  magic 14: load bufA         ← loads NEXT tiles [OVERLAP]
  magic 15b: writeback X      ← writes PREVIOUS FIN0 results [OVERLAP]
  sync PE

loop back to HALF_A
```

### Why overlaps are safe (no SPM conflicts)

- magic 15a reads P2_BUF_Y while PE writes P2_BUF_X → different regions
- magic 14 writes P2_BUF_Y input while PE reads FIN0_X → different regions
- magic 15b reads FIN0_Y while PE reads FIN0_X → different regions

### Prologue

Before entering the steady state, one PE P2 must complete so
the first magic 15a has results to read:

```
magic 14 bufA      → load first tiles
magic 14 bufB      → load second tiles
PE P2 bufB         → compute (provides data for HALF_A m15a)
```

### Drain

A drain counter tracks consecutive empty magic 14 calls. When
it reaches 4, exit to P2_END. Reset to 0 whenever tiles are loaded.

### Multipass

When FIN0 has too many arcs for one batch, magic 15a sets a
multipass flag. After PE FIN0 sync, a loop runs:
  magic 18 (writeback current pass) → magic 20 (load next batch) →
  PE FIN0 → spin → check flag → loop

### HA Bucket Consistency

magic 15b (writeback) must complete BEFORE magic 15a (load) runs
so that HA buckets in MM contain the latest keys. Place magic 15b
at the START of the PE P2 overlap, before magic 15a:

```
  set_PC PE_P2 bufA
  magic 15b: writeback Y      ← ensure MM has latest HA keys
  magic 15a: read bufB → X    ← loads HA from MM (now up to date)
```

### Magic Mask Assignments

| Half | PE P2     | m15b (wb prev) | m15a (load)       | PE FIN0   | m14 (load) |
|------|-----------|----------------|--------------------|-----------|------------|
| A    | PE_P2_BUF0| MAGIC_18_F0B   | MAGIC_15_BUF1_F0A | PE_FIN0_A | MAGIC_14_BUF1 |
| B    | PE_P2_BUF1| MAGIC_18_F0A   | MAGIC_15_BUF0_F0B | PE_FIN0_B | MAGIC_14_BUF0 |

Multipass within HALF_A uses MAGIC_18_F0A / MAGIC_20_F0A (current fX).
Multipass within HALF_B uses MAGIC_18_F0B / MAGIC_20_F0B (current fY).

## Steps to Implement

### 1. Verify non-overlapped baseline

Run `gwfa_check_correctness.py 3` (debug mode) with the current
non-overlapped code to generate golden wfDebug output. Save it
for comparison.

### 2. Write overlapped instruction generator

Replace the phase 2 section of `gwfa_instruction_generator.py`.
Use `f.write_count` to track PCs and `f.patch_imm0()` for all
forward branch offsets. No manual offset arithmetic.

### 3. Test with wfDebug comparison

Run correctness mode 3. Compare wfDebug.txt against golden. The
wavefront values at each step must match exactly. If they diverge,
the first mismatch shows which step/entry is wrong.

### 4. Run full 295

Run `gwfa_check_correctness.py -t 56 2` for all 295 queries.

## Files to Modify

- `scripts/gwfa_instruction_generator.py` — phase 2 section only
  (phase 1 unchanged, PE instructions unchanged)

## Files NOT to Modify

- `pe_array.cpp` — magic 14/15/18/20 handlers already support
  all mask combinations
- `pe.cpp` — PE magic 13/19 already support both P2 and FIN0
  buffer selections
- `sys_def.h` — SPM layout constants already defined
